      "value": "@{5e44a1bd0c91c2477a8b8acb|full_name}: That doesn't work for me. Here's a gif of a test upload with completely default playable layers, except with tracking control set to animation for the feet: https://gfycat.com/queasyyearlyamericanindianhorse\nEdit: Realized you probably meant auto footsteps *on* but with tracking control set to animation for the feet. In my reply above I thought you meant with it off. But, I've now tried it with auto footsteps on too and the problem is the same as with auto footsteps off. The body does not re-align with the head when you stop moving. Here's a gif for good measure - the first few seconds shows that I have auto footsteps on, then I change tracking control to animation for the feet and show that the issue is still there: https://gfycat.com/BreakableBiodegradableBlobfish\nFeet + hips (or just hips) also doesn't work if you just put it on animation. The only way I've managed to get the body to realign with the head is to set hip tracking to animation, then back to tracking (I set up a quick layer to toggle it on GestureRight = 1): https://gfycat.com/tediousscentedcaribou\nI tried all of the above with two completely different models just to be sure.",
